CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] .* leading pack: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] .* after a type: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] .* several packs: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] .* WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
The explicit arguments were bound positionally, one per parameter, so the
elements of the first pack spilled into the following (deduced) packs.
g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG
assertion.
